uilding on a novel hierarchical fashion, our method can achieve great efficiency, even at the most complex all-atom level. In addition, completeness at all levels enable models to generate informative and discriminative representations. Practically, ProNet possesses great flexibility for different data and downstream tasks. Users can easily choose the level of granularity at which the model should operate based on their data and tasks. We conduct experiments on multiple downstream tasks, including protein fold and function prediction, protein-ligand binding affinity prediction, and protein-protein interaction prediction. Results show that ProNet outperforms recent methods on most datasets. We also show that different data and tasks may require representations at different levels."
